  "synthesis": {
    "description": "A customer or an internal originator asks for a price on gas: a fuel buyer wants to lock in volumes for future months, a municipal gas authority contact is passed along, or a colleague forwards a spreadsheet of requirements or a deal and asks whether the desk is interested. The trader prices the request against the forward curve, calls the customer back and follows up with a quote or bid.",
    "steps": [
      "A customer or colleague sends a request for a bid, hedge or fixed forward price, often with a spreadsheet of volumes and months.",
      "The request is routed to the trader or marketer who covers that customer, sometimes with a contact report.",
      "The trader reviews the volumes, delivery points and term requested.",
      "The trader prices the request against current forward prices and any transport costs.",
      "The trader calls the customer and sends the quote or bid.",
      "The customer accepts, declines or comes back to follow up."
    ],
    "approach": "A shared quote request form capturing customer, delivery point, months and volumes, feeding a pricing sheet that pulls current forward prices and transport adders so the trader only reviews and adjusts the number before sending a standard quote.",
    "rationale": "Requests come in as free text, voice mail and spreadsheets in differing layouts; one intake and pricing layout removes the re-keying and lets the trader focus on the price decision.",
    "artifact_type": "template"
  },
